        <mxCell id="rb" value="ROLLBACK — stock untouched, no order row" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=11;fontColor=#B85450;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="880" width="420" height="20" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n1" value="ONE TRANSACTION

Placing an order writes to three tables and must be
all-or-nothing, so the whole method is a single unit
of work:

• SELECT … FOR UPDATE serialises concurrent orders for
  the same part, so two buyers cannot take the last unit.
• unit_price is copied onto the line item, fixing the
  invoice total at the moment of sale.
• Any failure rolls everything back — the order row and
  the stock decrement are never half-applied." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1420" y="120" width="380" height="230" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n2" value="Insufficient stock is a client error, not a bug:
it returns 409 Conflict as an RFC 7807 ProblemDetail
naming the part and the quantity available, so the
caller can correct the request." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1420" y="380" width="380" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
